# Product UI default (Linear system)

For **all** Batatis product UI / frontend / visual / UX work matching these globs:

1. **Look:** Follow `docs/design-system-calm.md` and `web/src/calm/`; use `.cursor/skills/batatis-ui-linear/SKILL.md` for P0 interaction rules. The historical charcoal look is superseded.
2. **UI P0:** Neutral grey primary CTAs (not indigo fill); active nav faint fill only; shared gap source; gate complete/download while gaps open; no demo leakage; styled controls; nowrap labels in wrapping rows (no clipping); previews show real values (no `[placeholder]` / `present`); every control wired (nav = links, no `alert()`); no silent defaults; one derived data model; no "Required" label without a shared gap; checkbox = true 14px square, checked light fill + dark check. Formal review uses a fresh independent reviewer under `.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`.
3. **Simplify ruthlessly without dropping capabilities.**
4. **Model:** GPT-6.1-Sol at max for UI implementation **and** independent UI review; `.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` is the shared model policy.
5. **Bug-free bar:** smoke `evals/ui-artifacts/smoke.mjs`; cite ≠ AI; confidence/no silent fills.
6. **Attribution:** portability ≠ SCO UX; process fields ≠ evidence ladder.
